<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Shakopee, Minn., $2.555 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $39.414 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $15.102 million GO water utility bonds.</p>
<p>--Newark, N.J., $5 million redevelopment bonds.</p>
<p>--Cobleskill-Rich Central School District, N.Y., $9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Johnsburg Central School District, N.Y., $3.05 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Methacton School District, Pa., $9.995 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Stewart County, Tenn., $8.1 million school bonds, by direct purchase.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
